-- title:
--   Two irreducible components in the mod p fibre of X₁(Mp)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and an integer $M \ge 5$ with $p \nmid M$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, with $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ which is assumed equal to $L$-adjoined to the image, under the coefficientwise embedding $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q} \to \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$, of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A \to L$, equipped with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $A \to L \to K$; let $j \in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion the image of the $q$-expansion $q^{-1}\cdot\mathrm{jNumQ}$ of the modular $j$-invariant, and let $\mathbb{Z}/p$ be an $A$-algebra. Then the pullback of the structure morphism $\mathrm{TwoChart.modelTo}\ A\ K\ j$ of the two-chart model (the pushout of the spectra of the $A$-subalgebras of $K$ generated by $j$ and by $j^{-1}$) along $\mathrm{Spec}(\mathbb{Z}/p) \to \mathrm{Spec}\,A$ admits two distinct irreducible components $Z_0 \ne Z_1$ such that every irreducible component equals $Z_0$ or $Z_1$.
--
--   This is the statement that the special fibre at $p$ of the two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ over $A = \mathbb{Z}_p[\zeta_p]$ has exactly two irreducible components, in the form of an existence of an exhaustive pair of distinct components (no identification of the individual components is made). It is used in the subsequent analysis of that special fibre: the decomposition of its components as $\mathbb{Z}/p$-curves forming a pullback square, the behaviour of the cusp sections, and the comparison of the images of the two components.
